MSP DisplayPort: send only what changed, for devices that clear at once

Betaflight's OSD sends CLEAR_SCREEN, then every element, then DRAW_SCREEN
on each frame, expecting the device to show the result at DRAW_SCREEN.
FETtec's G0 OSD chip on the T-Motor Pacer G4 Alpha Analog (an STM32G071
running FETtec's Alpha OSD 0.1.18, on UART4) acts on CLEAR_SCREEN as soon
as it arrives. With elements turned on, the OSD flickers at the default
12 Hz and the right side is worst. Timer 2, the vtx channel and throttle
never show: they come early in the draw order, so the clear probably wipes
them before the G0 shows them.

A grid of digits sent straight to the G0 stays steady when redrawn at 4 or
12 Hz without CLEAR_SCREEN, and blinks when redrawn at 4 Hz with
CLEAR_SCREEN first.

With USE_MSP_DISPLAYPORT_DIFF defined, the FC keeps the screen it wants and
the screen it has sent, and sends only the changed characters, with spaces
where text went away. CLEAR_SCREEN goes out only to resync: at start-up,
after a release, and on a redraw. One row is resent in full every frame, so
the device catches up after a lost string. CMS menus are flushed on commit,
since they never call DRAW_SCREEN. Without the define, the file builds as
before.

Tested 2026-11-16 on an Alpha Analog with a PAL camera: the OSD is steady,
and timer 2, the vtx channel and throttle all show. Settings saved before
the change survived it (`diff all` identical).

Applies to Betaflight 2026.6.2. From the root of the Betaflight source:

    patch -p1 < msp-displayport-diff.patch

